\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. As with gladness men of old
\par Did the guiding star behold,
\par As with joy they hailed its light,
\par Leading onward, beaming bright;
\par So, most gracious Lord, may we
\par Evermore be led to Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. As with joyful steps they sped,
\par Saviour, to Thy lowly bed,
\par There to bend the knee before
\par Thee, whom heaven and earth adore;
\par So may we with willing feet
\par Ever seek the mercy-seat.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. As they offered gifts most rare
\par At Thy cradle rude and bare;
\par So may we with holy joy,
\par Pure, and free from sin's alloy,
\par All our costliest treasures bring,
\par Christ, to Thee, our heavenly King.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Holy Jesus, every day
\par Keep us in the narrow way;
\par And, when earthly things are past,
\par Bring our ransomed souls at last
\par Where they need no star to guide,
\par Where no clouds Thy glory hide.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. In the heavenly country bright
\par Need they no created light;
\par Thou its light, its joy, its crown,
\par Thou its sun which goes not down;
\par There for ever may we sing
\par Hallelujahs to our King.
\par                               Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
